      ],
      "content": "TL 01 SW         NETTLEDEN WITH         FRITHSDEN                  POTTEN END             (North side) 3/196                                   No. 10 - -                                       II House.  C18  ('17TD33'  cut  in brick by ground  floor front window) replacing end bay of former C16/C17 house to W. Plum brick with red brick at quoins and window jambs, and steep old red tile roof. Timber framed W party wall with wattle and daub infill survives from earlier house. A small 2-storeys and attic house set back from road facing S with integral rear catslide outshut and entrance by door on E with gabled open timber porch. 3-light small-pane Yorkshire sliding casements with segmental arches. One window on each floor on S front, ground floor window, stair window, and small 2-light attic window on E. Interior of 2 bays with side-purlin roof, and roughly squared crossbeam and joists exposed. Exposed timber frame on W has jowled posts and clasped-purlins. Listing NGR: TL0126810005"
    }
